What is ASGI (Asynchronous Server Gateway Interface) and how does it differ from WSGI?
- they are gateway interface for python
- WSGI Web Server Gateway Interface: sync, blocking I/O, traditional HTTP -> simple web app with low traffic, not real-time feature
- ASGI Asyncronized Server Gateway Interface: async, non-blocking I/O, supports modern protocals and suitable for high-traffice, real-time appplication

How is FastAPI different from Flask?
- leverages asyncio for high performance
- well-established endpoint ->pydantic -> database paradigm
- flask is more like "do whatever you want", easy flexible but low performance, only use when you need a static or a very very basic dynamic page

Explain the difference between response_model, response_model_exclude, and response_model_include in FastAPI route decorators. When would you use each?
- response_model: when you want to define the structure and types of data to be return
- response_model_include: when you have comprehensive response_model and only what to return a subset of the fields
- response_model_exclude: when you have response_model and want to exlude specific fields

